---
import Layout from '~/layouts/Layout.astro';
import Header from '~/components/widgets/Header.astro';
import Footer from '~/components/widgets/Footer.astro';
import InlineGlossary from '~/components/blog/InlineGlossary.astro';
import { SITE } from '~/utils/config';
import { headerData, footerData } from '~/navigation';
---

<Layout 
  metadata={{
    title: 'SORA Glossary Demo | Inline Tooltips Example',
    description: 'Demonstration of inline SORA glossary tooltips in action.',
    url: `${SITE.site}/glossary-demo`,
    type: 'website'
  }}
>
  <Header {...headerData} isSticky showRssFeed showToggleTheme />
  
  <main class="py-8 sm:py-16 lg:py-20">
    <div class="container mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 max-w-4xl">
      <div class="text-center mb-12">
        <h1 class="text-4xl md:text-5xl font-bold leading-tighter tracking-tighter font-heading mb-6">
          SORA Glossary Demo
        </h1>
        <p class="text-xl md:text-2xl text-muted dark:text-slate-400 max-w-3xl mx-auto">
          Hover over the highlighted terms below to see instant definitions and learn more about the SORA ecosystem.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="prose prose-lg dark:prose-invert max-w-none">
        <h2>Understanding the SORA Ecosystem</h2>
        
        <p>
          The <InlineGlossary term="SORA" /> network represents a revolutionary approach to decentralized finance, 
          built on the foundation of <InlineGlossary term="Hyperledger Iroha" /> technology. 
          At its core, SORA utilizes an <InlineGlossary term="Elastic Supply" /> model for its primary token, 
          <InlineGlossary term="XOR" />, which automatically adjusts based on economic conditions.
        </p>

        <p>
          The ecosystem is governed by the <InlineGlossary term="SORA Parliament" />, where 
          <InlineGlossary term="VAL" /> token holders participate in democratic decision-making processes. 
          This governance system ensures that the network remains decentralized and community-driven.
        </p>

        <h3>DeFi and Trading</h3>
        
        <p>
          <InlineGlossary term="Polkaswap" /> serves as SORA's decentralized exchange, enabling 
          cross-chain trading and liquidity aggregation. Users can provide liquidity to 
          <InlineGlossary term="Liquidity Pool" />s and earn rewards through 
          <InlineGlossary term="Yield Farming" /> strategies.
        </p>

        <p>
          The <InlineGlossary term="Token Bonding Curve" /> mechanism ensures fair price discovery 
          for <InlineGlossary term="PSWAP" /> tokens, while the network's 
          <InlineGlossary term="Validator" />s secure the blockchain through 
          <InlineGlossary term="Staking" /> mechanisms.
        </p>

        <h3>Real-World Applications</h3>
        
        <p>
          SORAMITSU, the company behind SORA, has successfully deployed 
          <InlineGlossary term="CBDC" /> solutions like Cambodia's Bakong, demonstrating 
          the real-world viability of the technology. The upcoming 
          <InlineGlossary term="SORA v3" /> will integrate with 
          <InlineGlossary term="Polkadot" /> as a <InlineGlossary term="Parachain" />, 
          enabling enhanced cross-chain functionality.
        </p>

        <p>
          Developers can test new features on the <InlineGlossary term="Fujiwara Testnet" /> 
          before they're deployed to the mainnet, ensuring stability and security for all users.
        </p>

        <div class="bg-blue-50 dark:bg-blue-900/20 border border-blue-200 dark:border-blue-800 rounded-lg p-6 mt-8">
          <h4 class="text-lg font-semibold text-blue-900 dark:text-blue-100 mb-3">
            💡 How to Use This Feature
          </h4>
          <p class="text-blue-800 dark:text-blue-200">
            Simply hover over any highlighted term to see its definition instantly. 
            The tooltips are color-coded by category and include related terms and examples. 
            This makes complex SORA concepts accessible to both beginners and experts.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </main>

  <Footer {...footerData} />
</Layout>
